WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.252
Now consider what happens when the text cannot be converted to a number.

00:00:04.252 --> 00:00:07.352
The variable contains “abc”.

00:00:07.352 --> 00:00:14.437
Calling float on that text would fail because those characters do not represent a numeric value.

00:00:14.437 --> 00:00:17.967
The example performs a simple check first.

00:00:17.967 --> 00:00:26.028
It removes one decimal point if there is one, then uses isdigit to see whether the remaining characters are digits.

00:00:26.503 --> 00:00:34.094
With “abc”, the condition is false, so the program prints a warning instead of attempting the conversion.

00:00:34.094 --> 00:00:37.719
This is only a simple preview of validation.

00:00:37.719 --> 00:00:46.169
Real data can contain negative signs, spaces, commas, missing values, and other complications.

00:00:46.169 --> 00:00:50.832
The key idea is to check assumptions before trusting incoming data.
